# From code-shape-kit's templates/CODEOWNERS. With "Require review from Code
# Owners" on in the branch protection rules, a pull request that changes the
# code-shape rules can't be merged without the owner's approval: a red gate
# can't be turned green by loosening them.

# [tool.shape] (limits, banned APIs, output_modules, ...), [tool.importlinter]
# (memclaw's layout rules), [tool.vulture] and the pinned kit version
/pyproject.toml                         @emanuilo
# the baseline: known violations (memclaw's is empty)
/.code-shape/                           @emanuilo
# the hooks that run `code-shape check` before a commit (git and Claude Code)
/.githooks/                             @emanuilo
/.claude/settings.json                  @emanuilo
/.claude/hooks/                         @emanuilo
# the CI gate itself (the `shape` job)
/.github/workflows/ci.yml               @emanuilo
# this file
/.github/CODEOWNERS                     @emanuilo
